---
import InstallButtons from "../components/InstallButtons.astro";
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { loadData } from "../data/professors.ts";
import { CONTACT_EMAIL, CREATOR, DISCLAIMER } from "../data/site.ts";

const { totals } = loadData();
---

<Base
  title="What RowdySearch is"
  description="RowdySearch is a free lookup for UTSA professors and courses: official grade distributions, Bluebook evaluations, Rate My Professors ratings, and syllabi in one place.">
  <article class="prose mx-auto max-w-3xl">
    <h1 class="mb-4 text-3xl font-bold sm:text-4xl">What RowdySearch is</h1>

    <p>
      RowdySearch is a free tool for choosing professors at the University of Texas at San Antonio
      (UTSA). Search a professor, a course, or a subject, and it shows what you would otherwise have
      to collect from four different places.
    </p>

    <h2>What it shows</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Grade distributions.</strong> How many students got each grade in every section, from UTSA's own records.</li>
      <li><strong>Bluebook evaluations.</strong> UTSA's end-of-semester ratings of the instructor and the course, out of 5.</li>
      <li><strong>Rate My Professors.</strong> The rating, difficulty, would-take-again percentage, and recent reviews.</li>
      <li><strong>Syllabi.</strong> Links to each section's syllabus on Simple Syllabus.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      It covers {totals.professors.toLocaleString("en-US")} professors and {totals.courses.toLocaleString("en-US")} courses.{" "}
      <a href="/data/">Where the data comes from</a>
    </p>

    <h2>Why it exists</h2>
    <p>
      Picking a class means spending months with its professor. Before registering, students look the
      professor up on Rate My Professors, then find the syllabus, then go looking for grade data,
      which UTSA does not publish. RowdySearch puts all of it in one search.
    </p>
    <p>
      The grade data is the part that matters most. It shows whether a professor is hard or the
      course is hard, because every professor's grades sit beside the grades for the whole course.
    </p>

    <h2>The site and the extension</h2>
    <p>
      This site works in any browser, on a phone or a computer, with nothing to install. The
      extension, for Chrome and Firefox, puts the same lookup on UTSA's registration pages.{" "}
      <a href="/extension/">See what the extension does</a>
    </p>
    <InstallButtons />

    <h2>Who made it</h2>
    <p>
      RowdySearch was created by {CREATOR}. It is free, has no ads, and has no accounts. Questions
      and corrections go to <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>.
    </p>
    <p>{DISCLAIMER}</p>
  </article>
</Base>
